nes place), which is 0. The second step is 21 × 80 (tens place). Wait, but 80 is the entire tens place value here. Alternatively, maybe breaking down 80 as 8 tens, so 21 × 8 × 10. Let me see.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps the steps should be:.\n\n1. Multiply 21 by 0 (the ones digit), resulting in 0.\n\n2. Multiply 21 by 80 (the tens place value, since 8 is in the tens place, so 8×10=80). .\n\nThen sum those two results: 0 + (21×80). But 21×80 can be calculated as 21×8×10</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
