ght, so following the example\'s structure, let me outline the reasoning steps properly:\n\n1. Multiply 21 by the ones place digit (6) of 66: 21 × 6 = 126.\n\n2. Multiply 21 by the tens place digit (60) of 66: 21 × 60 = 1260.\n\nThen sum those two results: 126 + 1260 = 1386.\n\nSo the final answer should be 1386. I need to make sure each step is clear and follows the template\'s structure.\n</think>', '']
