iplication as written, the second digit (the tens place) is 9, so I multiply 99 by 9, but then shift it one place to the left. So that would also be 891 shifted left, so 8910. .\n\nNow, adding the two results together: 891 (from the ones place) and 8910 (from the tens place). Adding them: 891 + 8910</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
