Hmm, 59 times 2 is 118, so times 10 would be 1180? Wait, no, wait. Wait, 20 is 2*10, so 59*2 is 118, then times 10 gives 1180? Wait, but 59*20 is actually 1180? Let me check that again. Wait, 59*20: 59*2 is 118, so moving the decimal over, yes, 1180. Okay, that seems right.\n\nNow, adding the two results: 472 (from the ones place) and 1180 (from the tens place). Adding them together: 472 + 1180</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
