at's the second part.\n\nNow, since there are only two digits in 83, there's no hundreds place, so I don't have any more steps. The example had three steps because the number was three digits, but here we just have two. .\n\nNow I need to add the results of these two steps together. So adding 279 and 7440. Let's see, 279 + 7440. Adding the units: 9 +0=9, 7+4=11, 2+4=6 plus the carried over 1 makes 7, and then 7 remains. Wait, maybe I should do it more straightforwardly</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
