t down step by step according to the template.\n\nFirst, since 37 has two digits, we can split the multiplication into two parts: the ones place (7) and the tens place (30).\n\nStep 1: Multiply 26 by the ones digit (7):\n26 \u00d7 7 = (20 \u00d7 7) + (6 \u00d7 7) = 140 + 42 = 182.\n\nStep 2: Multiply 26 by the tens digit (30):\n26 \u00d7 30 = (26 \u00d7 3) \u00d7 10 = 78 \u00d7 10 = 780.\n\nNow, add the results of both steps:\n182 (from step 1) + 780 (from step 2) = 962.\n\nTherefore, the correct product is 962, not 961 as initially thought. The error might have occurred during addition or multiplication steps. It's important to carefully check each step to avoid such mistakes.\n</think>\n\n",
